"""SWD header: bare through-hole pads at 1.27 mm pitch for an ST-Link's SWD lines, and optionally
its supply pin.

Default: three pads, 1 GND, 2 SWDIO, 3 SWCLK: the middle three contacts of boards/main's SWD
connector P1 (1 SWD_VDD, 2 GND, 3 SWDIO, 4 SWCLK, 5 NRST) in the same order, without NRST.
With `supply`: four pads in the 4-pin order of a clone ST-Link's 1.27 mm SWD lead (owner,
2026-11-01): 1 SWDIO, 2 GND, 3 SWCLK, 4 VDD, VDD taking the probe's 5 V pin into the board (the
board decides what that pin feeds; main2 takes it through a Schottky diode into its regulators'
input). The lead plugs on pin 1 to pad 1; turned round, or shifted one pad either way, the probe's
5 V never lands on the board's GND. The two variants number their pads differently: a board
switching variants re-routes the header.

Footprints: KiCad's PinHeader_1x03_P1.27mm_Vertical and PinHeader_1x04_P1.27mm_Vertical
(kicad-footprint-generator, connector/pin_header_socket) with their 1.0 mm pads grown to 1.05 mm,
square pad 1 with the silkscreen's pin-1 corner beside it, on 0.65 mm drills at 1.27 mm pitch: a
0.2 mm ring against JLCPCB's 0.18 mm PTH minimum and 0.22 mm between pads (rules/jlcpcb.kicad_dru).
The pads are numbered along the row; the symbols map the signals onto them. No part is placed: a
1.27 mm pitch header (or the probe's wires) is soldered by hand, so the header is excluded from the
BOM and the placement file. Each footprint embeds KiCad's model of its header all the same, so the
layout's height checks see the soldered header.
"""

prefix = config(str, default="J", help="Reference designator prefix")
supply = config(bool, default=False, help="four pads in a clone ST-Link's order, 1 SWDIO, 2 GND, 3 SWCLK, 4 VDD")

GND = io(Ground)
SWDIO = io(Net)
SWCLK = io(Net)
VDD = io(Power, optional=True, help="pad 4, with supply = True: the probe's supply pin")

pins = {"GND": GND, "SWDIO": SWDIO, "SWCLK": SWCLK}
if supply:
    pins["VDD"] = VDD

Component(
    name="J",
    prefix=prefix,
    symbol=Symbol(library="SwdHeader.kicad_sym", name="SwdHeader4" if supply else "SwdHeader"),
    pins=pins,
    skip_bom=True,
    skip_pos=True,
)
